            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"A period of seven years (a 'heptad' of years) in prophetic literature, and more broadly, a symbol of divine completeness and perfect timing.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Daniel 9:24-27\",\"Genesis 29:27-28\",\"Leviticus 25:8\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"A symbol of perfection, rest, and the complete cycle of divine creation.\",\"basis\":[\"Genesis 2:1-3\",\"Exodus 20:11\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"An indefinite, qualitative era of church history, divine action, or tribulation rather than a strict mathematical calculation of years.\",\"basis\":[\"Daniel 9:24-27\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"},{\"meaning\":\"A literal period of seven consecutive days.\",\"basis\":[\"Genesis 1\",\"Daniel 10:2-3\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The Hebrew word for week, 'shavua', literally means a 'seven' or a 'heptad'. In the context of Daniel's Seventy Weeks, there is a strong consensus across both dispensational and covenantal frameworks that these refer to weeks of years (seven years per week). Broadly, the week is tied to the number seven, representing fullness, completion, and the Sabbath cycle.\"}",
